@NODE iNTRODUCTiON "iNTRODUCTiON OF OFF-LiNE-FiLE-MOVER VERSiON 0.2"

!!! ATTENTiON !!!

THiS TOOL iS ONLY USEFULL FOR SYSOPS WHO RUN AMi EXPRESS!

OFF-LiNE-FiLE-MOVER iS A SMALL TOOL WHiCH WiLL BE STARTED FROM THE LOG-
OFF BATCH OR SiMPLY FROM CLi. iT MOVES OLD FiLES FROM YOUR UPLOAD-
DiRECTORY TO ANOTHER DiRECTORY (OFF-LiNE) AND CREATES THE DiR-FiLES NEW.

ALSO iT HAS @{"FEATURES" LiNK FEATURES} THAT OTHER TOOLS DOESN'T HAVE.

@ENDNODE

@NODE FEATURES "FEATURES OF OFF-LiNE-FiLE-MOVER VERSiON 0.2"

i DECiDED TO CODE THiS TOOL, BECAUSE iT iS TOO BORiNG TO COPY FiLES BY
HAND FROM ONE DiRECTORY TO ANOTHER. WELL, THERE ARE SOME FiLE-MOVERS
ARROUND, BUT THEY WORK NOT 100% SiNCE SOME FAKERS AND NUKERS PUT
ANSi-CODES iNTO THE DiR-FiLE. THEY CRASHES MOST TiME WHEN DETECTiNG
ANSi-CODES iN THE DiR-FiLES. MiNE DOES NOT. iT iS FAST, DOES NOT
CRASH AND MAKES BACK-UP FiLES OF THE OLD DiR-FiLES. iF YOU DON'T WANT
TO BUiLT OFF-LiNE-FiLE-MOVER iNTO YOU LOG-OFF-BATCH THEN YOU ALSO
CAN START iT FROM CLi.

NOW i THiNK i GAVE YOU ENOUGH REASONS TO USE MY TOOL. HAVE FUN ANYWAYS.

@ENDNODE

@NODE iNSTALLATiON "iNSTALLATiON OF OFF-LiNE-FiLE-MOVER VERSiON 0.2"

JUST COPY THE FiLES FROM THE LHA-ARCHiEVE iNTO YOUR FAVOURiTE DiRECTORY AND
ADD iT TO YOUR LOG-OFF-BATCH SO iT WiLL BE STARTED WHENEVER SOMEBODY iS
LOGGiNG OFF YOUR BBS. iF YOU DON'T WANT TO DO THAT, YOU CAN ALSO START iT
FROM THE CLi.

MAKE SURE THAT YOU HAVE THE FOLLOWiNG FiLES LOCATED iN YOUR C-DiRECTORY:

1. COPY
2. DELETE
3. MOVE

WiTHOUT THESE FiLES OFF-LiNE-FiLE-MOVER WON'T WORK!


THATS ALL.

@ENDNODE

@NODE CONFiG "HOW TO EDiT THE CONFiG-FiLE OF OFF-LiNE-FiLE-MOVER V0.2 ?"

OFF-LiNE-FiLE-MOVER CALLED 'OFFLiNE.CFG'. COPY THiS FiLE ALSO iNTO THE
DiRECTORY WHERE THE MAiNPROGRAM iS LOCATED. iF YOU DO NOT DO THAT,
OFF-LiNE-FiLE-MOVER WON'T WORK.

HERE ARE THE CONTENTS OF THE CONFiG-FiLE:


 1st LiNE: ' 24  '                    <-- THiS iS THE AMOUNT OF DAYS
                                          THE FiLES SHOULD STAY ONLiNE
                                          iN YOUR UPLOAD-DiRECTORY.

                                          E.G.: '30' MEANS THAT EVERY
                                          FiLE THAT iS OLDER THAN 30
                                          DAYS, WiLL MOVED OFF-LiNE.


 2nd LiNE: ' BBS:AMIGA/DIR2 '         <-- THiS iS THE LOCATiON OF THE
                                          DiR-FiLE FROM YOUR UPLOAD-
                                          DiRECTORY.


 3rd LiNE: ' BBS:AMIGA/UPLOAD/ '      <-- THiS iS THE PATH OF YOUR
                                          UPLOAD-DiRECTORY.


 4th LiNE: ' BBS:AMIGA/OFFLINE/ '     <-- THiS iS THE PATH WHERE THE
                                          FiLES WiLL BE MOVED iF THEiR
                                          UPLOAD-DATE WiLL BE EXCEED BY
                                          THE AMOUNT OF DAYS GiVEN iN
                                          THE FiRST LiNE OF THiS CONFiG-
                                          FiLE.



 THAT SHOULD BE ALL FOR NOW...

@ENDNODE       

